bevy-horizon: reserve the submission's tail with each batch of GPFIFO entries

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at 953fa75a, after 0001-0029. scripts/build_nvk.sh applies it; this text before the first
"diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

nouveau_horizon_channel_exec_locked reserved a batch's entries with no tail, so a batch could
fill the GPFIFO up to the final skid, and the submit after it could then fail with NO_SPACE
("channel submit failed: no queue space"), which NVK turns into a lost device. It now keeps 3
entries for the submission's fence, report and cross-channel wait.

The change is nebadasSwifty's, from masseffect-nx's NVK patch
(https://github.com/nebadasSwifty/masseffect-nx, mesa/mesa-switch-masseffect.patch;
MIT, as its THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md puts its mesa/ changes), which saw the failure
on this base.

diff --git a/src/nouveau/horizon/nouveau_horizon_channel.c b/src/nouveau/horizon/nouveau_horizon_channel.c
index 512a3f7..dddf66f 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/horizon/nouveau_horizon_channel.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/horizon/nouveau_horizon_channel.c
@@ -1852,9 +1852,15 @@ nouveau_horizon_channel_exec_locked(
    const struct nouveau_horizon_exec *execs)
 {
    const uint32_t acquire_entries = channel->cache_acquire_emitted ? 0 : 2;
+   /* Leave room for the submission's tail too: submit_locked adds its fence
+    * and report entries (up to 2) and a cross-channel wait (1) after the
+    * final skid. Reserving the skid alone let a batch fill the GPFIFO to it,
+    * and the submit that followed failed with NO_SPACE, which NVK turns into
+    * a lost device. From masseffect-nx's NVK patch.
+    */
    enum nouveau_horizon_status status =
       nouveau_horizon_channel_reserve_entries_locked(
-         channel, exec_count + acquire_entries, 0);
+         channel, exec_count + acquire_entries, 3);
    if (status != NOUVEAU_HORIZON_SUCCESS)
       goto done;
 
